[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `h` (parity) | `flips = h / 2` — for odd `h` the middle row is never touched | even, odd |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `h` (magnitude) | `i < flips` gate | 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, many |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `w` | `j < w` gate and the row stride `w*i` | 0, 1, 2, many |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `pix` contents | swap is value-moving; value-dependent bugs only show with varied bytes | randomized per row, all 4 channels distinct |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | buffer slack | reading/writing exactly `w*h` pixels vs. touching beyond | guard bytes appended after `w*h` and checked for both |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | row overlap | `a` and `b` alias when `w*i == w*(h-i-1)`, i.e. impossible for `i < h/2`; adjacent rows (`h == 2,3`) are the closest case | `h` = 2, 3 |
