[1mPhase A artifacts[22m (in [38;5;10mtranslation/[0m): [38;5;10mSYMBOLS.md[0m (1 symbol, diff empty), [38;5;10mERRORS.md[0m (15 rows), [38;5;10mCONFIGS.md[0m (28 rows). Row counts match test counts one-to-one (28 [38;5;10mphase_b_row*[0m tests, 15 [38;5;10mphase_c_row*[0m tests).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mThe bug I found and fixed.[22m The Rust used [38;5;10mptr::offset[0m/[38;5;10mptr::add[0m and [38;5;10mcore::ptr::swap[0m. Those carry debug-only "unsafe precondition" assertions that abort the process when the address calculation overflows or leaves the allocation — conditions the C reaches routinely and never traps on. With [38;5;10mw = h = 65536[0m the C's [38;5;10mw * (h-i-1)[0m overflows [38;5;10mint[0m to [38;5;10m-65536[0m and it just dereferences the wrapped address; the Rust aborted instead. Negative [38;5;10mw[0m hit the same check. The translation now uses [38;5;10mwrapping_offset[0m/[38;5;10mwrapping_add[0m and a literal [38;5;10mlet t = *a; *a = *b; *b = t;[0m, so behavior is identical in both build profiles. Confirmed: all fault cases now give SIGSEGV(11) in both C and Rust.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mOne documented, irreducible difference.[22m In a [3mdebug[23m Rust build, Rust's null-pointer UB check turns a null dereference into SIGABRT(6) where C gives SIGSEGV(11). That's a Rust debugging feature the C cannot have. The harness therefore loads [38;5;10mtarget/release/libflip_horizontal_lib.so[0m — the artifact [38;5;10mcargo build --release[0m ships and that a [38;5;10mdlopen[0m consumer would load — and holds it to exact signal equality. The debug artifact passes everything except those two null-deref rows; that allowance is only granted when [38;5;10mHARVEST_RUST_SO[0m explicitly points elsewhere.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mNon-vacuity.[22m Because a one-function library with no error channel makes it easy to write tests that pass for the wrong reason, I added [38;5;10mscripts/mutation_check.sh[0m: six deliberately-wrong builds (unsigned [38;5;10mh/2[0m, off-by-one row pairing, dropped alpha, short inner loop, extra flip, [38;5;10mj != w[0m). All six are rejected by the suite. I also confirmed the four fault cases genuinely segfault rather than silently exiting 0.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Two things worth flagging. [38;5;10mCargo.toml[0m declares no [38;5;10m[features][0m table, so "every feature combination" is only [38;5;10mdefault[0m and [38;5;10m--no-default-features[0m; [38;5;10mscripts/verify_all.sh[0m enumerates the powerset generically so it stays correct if features are added. And the "compare C and Rust binary stdout" gate is not applicable — neither build produces an executable — which [38;5;10mphase_b_no_binary_target[0m asserts structurally so the claim fails loudly rather than going stale, as does the no-enum claim behind [38;5;10mERRORS.md[0m row 15. Nothing in [38;5;10mc_src/[0m was modified.[0m[0m
